<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Sign-in required — Host Build Gateway</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/soe.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="topbar">
    <div class="topbar-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="0.5" y="0.5" width="13" height="3" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
                <rect x="0.5" y="5.5" width="13" height="3" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
                <rect x="0.5" y="10.5" width="9" height="3" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
            </svg>
            Host Build
        </a>
    </div>
</header>
<main>
    <section class="masthead">
        <p class="eyebrow">Access</p>
        <h1>Sign-in required</h1>
        <p>Every surface in this platform is scoped to a Keycloak realm role, so single
           sign-on has to be installed before <span class="mono">{{surface}}</span> can be
           opened. This is deliberate — role scoping is enforced on the server, not hidden
           in the interface.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="note note-warn">
        <strong>Install SSO</strong>
        <p><code>composer nimbus:add-keycloak {{installer_name}}</code></p>
        <p>This creates the realm, the client, the four persona roles
           (<code>app-owner</code>, <code>requester</code>, <code>customer</code>,
           <code>team-member</code>) and one demo user per persona.</p>
        <p>Reveal the generated passwords with
           <code>composer nimbus:vault-view {{installer_name}}</code>.</p>
    </div>
</main>
<footer>Host Build — Order &amp; Tracking Gateway · {{installer_name}}</footer>
</body>
</html>
